<title>USA: Chester Valley Bancorp Q3 net increases.</title>
<headline>Chester Valley Bancorp Q3 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>DOWNINGTOWN, Pa. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended   Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					 March 31,	     March 31,</p>
<p>				  1997	1996	1997	1996</p>
<p>Net Interest income	2,706     2,432     8,094     7,193</p>
<p>Provision for possible loan losses</p>
<p>				    97	  62	 357	 247</p>
<p>SAIF special assessment    ---	 ---     1,387	 ---</p>
<p>Net income		    $729	$641    $1,186    $1,838</p>
<p>Earnings per common share</p>
<p>    Primary		  $0.35     $0.31     $0.58     $0.89</p>
<p>    Fully Diluted	  $0.35     $0.31     $0.58     $0.89</p>
<p>(Dollars in Thousands Except for Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said the third quarter period ended March 31. Per share amounts have been restated to reflect the effects of the five percent stock dividend paid in September 1996 and the March 1997 five-for-four stock split effected in the form of a dividend.</p>
<p>Earnings for the nine-month period ended March 31, 1997, were $2.06 million, or $1.00 per share, excluding the one-time SAIF special assessment and adding back the effect of the premium reduction from $0.23 per $100 of deposits to $0.0648, compared to $1.84 million, or $0.89 per share, for the same period in 1996.</p>
</text>
